&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Senior Manager, EMEA Programmes &amp;amp; Campaigns, the Senior Marketing Campaigns Manager, Executive Audiences, will lead the strategy and execution of &lt;strong&gt;integrated marketing programmes&lt;/strong&gt; designed to engage senior executive audiences, accelerate pipeline growth, market expansion, and account penetration across EMEA&#39;s most strategic accounts. This role is critical to scaling Databricks&#39; growth in strategic industries and will oversee the planning, coordination, and tracking of EMEA-wide marketing initiatives across a variety of channels and tactics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the EMEA Marketing Campaigns team, you will own the Executive audience strategy and journey across the region. You will collaborate closely with EMEA Sales leadership, regional field marketing, global demand generation, Executive and industry product marketing, digital, marketing operations, customer marketing, partners, sales and other teams to shape and deliver cohesive, impactful programmes, experiences and go-to-market motions that resonate with C-level audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities will include driving key marketing programmes, ensuring alignment and consistency across the region, and developing scalable tools and frameworks to enhance EMEA Marketing efforts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute the EMEA executive audience strategy, aligned to EMEA pipeline and revenue goals, adapting global campaigns and programmes to EMEA priorities and driving awareness, engagement, and conversion across target accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design end-to-end Executive journeys across the customer lifecycle, collaborating with global marketing, customer marketing, paid digital, partners and other cross-functional teams, to connect the right content, experiences and touchpoints to build relationships, accelerate opportunities and support expansion, across technology and business executives, including CIOs, CTOs, CDOs, CISOs, CMOs and CFOs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and scale high-impact executive programmes, including Executive Forums, CIO Forums, executive roundtables, briefings, thought leadership content, and other high-touch experiences, leveraging customers and partners to strengthen credibility and engagement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with EMEA Sales and regional marketing teams to identify priority accounts and executives, and align executive engagement with account strategies and active sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure, monitor and optimise performance and business impact, using campaign, executive engagement and sales funnel data to identify opportunities, address coverage gaps and continuously improve programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable frameworks and best practices that enable regional teams to activate executive marketing across markets, ensuring consistency and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong B2B marketing experience working in the tech sector, in a fast-growing, fast-paced environment and a track record of developing programmes for senior executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learner mindset: The ability to learn new technologies, products and systems quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No detail is too small mentality: Strong project management skills to effectively deliver complex programmes working across multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-first approach: Ability to decipher data and build presentations around regular reporting that illustrate programme performance and insights across all demand channels.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone everyone is excited to work with: Strong interpersonal and communication skills to build collaborative relationships and create alignment with team members and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous and self-determined: Can easily balance multiple projects and timelines at once, has excellent attention to detail, and is seen as someone who gets things done.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritise and achieve in an environment that requires fresh thinking and new ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong growth mindset, having an open mind to new ideas and growth opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
